  "Wang Lung (to O-lan): \"I have been a fool and a fool. I shall buy love for her and I shall buy jewels for the little heart and I shall give it all to her and I will give nothing to the other slave.\"",
  "[action] Wang Lung takes money from the wall.",
  "[action] Wang Lung leaves his family and goes to a shop.",
  "[action] Wang Lung buys a red paper lantern.",
  "[action] Wang Lung buys red paper lantern.",
  "[action] Wang Lung gives the lantern to O-lan.",
  "Wang Lung: \"Here is a lantern to light your room at night, and here is red paper to paste upon your doors. Here is a little silver for the little heart. There is a little gold in my chest for a necklace and a little more in the wall for another necklace. There is a little more for a little more. There is gold enough for a hundred little hearts.\"",
